# Rank 1009 / CVE-2026-44643: angular-expressions remote code execution through
# filters. compile("a | __proto__")({}, {}) escapes the expression sandbox: the
# filter name is resolved against JavaScript objects without rejecting
# prototype-sensitive names, and the generated code reaches the Function
# constructor, giving arbitrary code execution (CWE-95, CWE-1321). The pool
# commit was a post-1.5.2 follow-up ("Allow enum of SyntaxType for
# disabledSyntaxes"), not the fix; corrected to 026afe7 ("Improve security
# hardening layers"), the core of the 1.5.1 -> 1.5.2 hardening series that
# blocks __proto__ property keys, protects the Function.prototype.constructor
# descriptor, and iterates with null-prototype contexts.
#
# ATTENTION, no precise generic detection for this repository.
#  - The vulnerable code is the evaluator's own sandbox internals (an AST
#    compiler that generates code strings plus filter resolution). A binding
#    that matched this repository's ASTCompiler shape would be repro-shaped:
#    answerable only to this CVE, not to library documentation, so the next
#    variant walks past it. The existing evaluator concept
#    code.ExpressionEvaluatorPrototypeNameAccess (VYQL-INJ-167) is bound to a
#    different evaluator library's tokens (type===IVAR, expr.functions) and does
#    not match this one.
#  - The generic, documentation-derivable detection for this class is
#    consumer-side: angular-expressions compile(untrusted)() is a code
#    evaluation sink like eval. That does not fire on the library's own
#    repository, which defines compile rather than calling it on untrusted
#    input, so it cannot detect this rank's vulnerable code. compile is not yet
#    modelled as a code-eval sink, so a consumer passing untrusted input is not
#    flagged either.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-precision-cost

test "rank1009: compiling an attacker-controlled angular expression is code execution"
  lang javascript
  file consumer.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-003
  code
  ```
  const expressions = require("angular-expressions");

  function render(req, res) {
    const template = req.query.expr;
    const result = expressions.compile(template)({}, {});
    res.send(String(result));
  }
  ```

test "rank1009: compiling a fixed trusted expression is not attacker-controlled"
  lang javascript
  file consumer.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-003
  code
  ```
  const expressions = require("angular-expressions");

  function render(req, res) {
    const result = expressions.compile("user.name | uppercase")({ user: { name: "a" } }, {});
    res.send(String(result));
  }
  ```
